line	<str>Go to the HAM lair west of Lumbridge Castle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick the lock on the trapdoor and enter the lair.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate south of the ladder to find the stolen silverware.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring the silverware to the Duke. He will fire Sigmund and give you a signed peace treaty.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Go into the basement again. Follow <col=800000>Kazgar</col> to travel to Mistag.</col>
step	23	-	Quick guide step 23
line	<str>Talk to Sigmund on the uk=1 of the Lumbridge Castle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Ask the following people about what happened in the cellar. You can stop when one mentions a goblin in the basement.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Duke Horacio again. ( if started Dragon Slayer)</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb-down the trapdoor in the kitchen on the uk=0.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your pickaxe on the rubble in the basement and climb through the hole.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light your light source and grab the brooch which sits on the floor about 10 steps into cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Show the brooch to the duke. or or</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Varrock Palace library in Varrock.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Reldo. or if not started shield of Arrav</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase on the west wall for goblin symbol book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read through the book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Goblin Village and talk to the generals, and mediate for them until you learn goblin emotes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back to the Lumbridge Castle cellar and follow the map in the image on this page through the caves. Don't stray from it! (Clicking on the minimap also auto-paths the correct path)</str>
line	
line	<str>At the end of the cave talk to Mistag, and do your Goblin Bow in front of him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Mistag then let him take you back to Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the duke. He won't believe you. or</str>
line	
line	<str>Pickpocket Sigmund and unlock his chest in the other room to find some HAM robes. Keep them for Death to the Dorgeshuun.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the HAM lair west of Lumbridge Castle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick the lock on the trapdoor and enter the lair.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate south of the ladder to find the stolen silverware.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring the silverware to the Duke. He will fire Sigmund and give you a signed peace treaty.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the basement again. Follow Kazgar to travel to Mistag.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to Mistag, with the peace treaty in your inventory, and a cutscene will play.</col>
